encil, and ballpoint pen on board","CreditLine":"The Jean Pigozzi African Art Collection.  Gift of Jean Pigozzi","URL":"https://www.moma.org/collection/works/299232","ImageURL":"https://www.moma.org/media/W1siZiIsIjQ2MTE3NiJdLFsicCIsImNvbnZlcnQiLCItcmVzaXplIDEwMjR4MTAyNFx1MDAzZSJdXQ.jpg?sha=64d03aa296982222"},{"ObjectID":401614,"Title":"Untitled, Chicago, Illinois","Artist":"Gordon Parks","Date":"1957","Medium":"Inkjet print, printed 2019","CreditLine":"The Family of Man Fund","URL":"https://www.moma.org/collection/works/401614","ImageURL":"https://www.moma.org/media/W1siZiIsIjQ3NzY4NCJdLFsicCIsImNvbnZlcnQiLCItcmVzaXplIDEwMjR4MTAyNFx1MDAzZSJdXQ.jpg?sha=fc9b0d76b84d49b2"},{"ObjectID":423482,"Title":"Studies for an Antifascist Memorial","Artist":"Bogdan Bogdanović","Date":"1960–1970","Medium":"Ink on mylar","CreditLine":"Gift of Alice and Tom Tisch","URL":"https://www.moma.org/collection/works/423482","ImageURL":"https://www.moma.org/media/W1siZiIsIjUwMDI0NiJdLFsicCIsImNvbnZlcnQiLCItcmVzaXplIDEwMjR4MTAyNFx1MDAzZSJdXQ.jpg?sha=9eee16e09a7864af"},{"ObjectID":434416,"Title":"Les fleurs du mal (The Flowers of Evil)","Artist":"Félix Bracquemond","Date":"Published 1857 (poems c. 1840–57); additional materials c. 1856–1919; rebound c. 1891","Medium":"Book with letterpress text; rebound with additional materials, most related to a planned but unrealized illustrated edition of Les fleurs du mal: a printed essay by Octave Uzanne (1891); six original etchings and one pencil and ink drawing by Bracquemond for the frontispiece; two sets of thirty-three wood engravings of typographic ornaments by Sotain after designs by Bracquemond; five handwritten letters among Baudelaire, Poulet-Malassis, Bracquemond, and Champfleury (1856–91); one gravure reproduction of an 1861 photograph of Baudelaire by Nadar; one etching by Bracquemond (portrait of Baudelaire, frontispiece for the 1861 second edition); three sale catalogue clippings. Bespoke rebinding and enclosure by Meunier for Samuel Putnam Avery. Rebinding: Full brown goat leather with leather onlays, gold tooling, stamping, painted details, purple satin flyleaves, marbled endpapers, gilt and gauffered page edges, and sterling silver skull clasps. Matching enclosure with built-in inner doors: brown goat leather with tooling and stamping on spine edge, decorated interior doors, gilded brass bosses with hidden lock pin, and red satin lining","CreditLine":"Gift of Helen and Sam Zell","URL":"https://www.moma.org/collection/works/434416","ImageURL":"https://www.moma.org/media/W1siZiIsIjYyNzkwNiJdLFsicCIsImNvbnZlcnQiLCItcmVzaXplIDEwMjR4MTAyNFx1MDAzZSJdXQ.jpg?sha=67d5b23401408d97","OnView":1},{"ObjectID":438392,"Title":"Lessons in Posing Subjects/Maintaining Facial Expressions (Male)","Artist":"Robert Heinecken","Date":"1981","Medium":"Five color instant prints (Polaroid SX-70) and letterpress text","CreditLine":"Gift of Anthony Allen","URL":"https://www.moma.org/collection/works/438392","ImageURL":"https://www.moma.org/media/W1siZiIsIjUyOTU5NiJdLFsicCIsImNvbnZlcnQiLCItcmVzaXplIDEwMjR4MTAyNFx1MDAzZSJdXQ.jpg?sha=5a0942877251d53a"},{"ObjectID":444356,"Title":"Tropical Night","Artist":"Christopher Cozier","Date":"2006-14","Medium":"1 of 268 sheets with acrylic, ink, colored ink, pencil, and colored pencil on paper, some with stamped ink, stencil, solvent transfer, and cut-and-pasted colored and painted paper","CreditLine":"Latin American and Caribbean Fund and Fund for the Twenty-First Century","URL":"https://www.moma.org/collection/works/444356","ImageURL":"https://www.moma.org/media/W1siZiIsIjU0MDcwMyJdLFsicCIsImNvbnZlcnQiLCItcmVzaXplIDEwMjR4MTAyNFx1MDAzZSJdXQ.jpg?sha=2491ab289a24bf28"},{"ObjectID":501014,"Title":"Martin Luther King Jr. with John Lewis and Andrew Young","Artist":"Steve Schapiro","Date":"1965","Medium":"Gelatin silver print","CreditLine":"Gift of the Estate of Steve Schapiro","URL":"https://www.moma.org/collection/works/501014","ImageURL":"https://www.moma.org/media/W1siZiIsIjYxMzEyOSJdLFsi